 8801736, "raw_content": "", "author": "Eruditio", "created": 1787835340233, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "www.dailywire.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATV3NfGC6.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://www.dailywire.com/news/he-was-jailed-for-exposing-muslim-violence-in-nigeria-now-hes-warning-americans-to-fight-sharia", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "A Nigerian journalist imprisoned for reporting on Christian persecution says Americans must fight the rise of Islam in the United States if they want to preserve their freedom.", "last_comment_created": 1787835340233, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 0, "score_up": 32, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "A Nigerian journalist imprisoned for reporting on Christian persecution says Americans must fight the rise of Islam in the United States if they want to preserve their freedom.Luka Binniyat issued the warning while speaking about a five-year legal battle that saw him spend over 80 days in prison after officials took issue with a story he wrote on an attack on a Christian village by Islamic militants. Binniyat, from the religiously divided, mineral-rich Nigerian state of Kaduna, is haunted by the violence he has witnessed.\u201cYou should not allow Islam to gain root in America. They\u2019ll come there with values that are not your own, and even if they are a minority, they will eventually try to enforce their own religion, their own beliefs over the community,\u201d the 60-year-old Binniyat told The Daily Wire in an interview. \u201cIn Nigeria \