ay, Digital and TV Digital ad spending reaches over $30 Billion dollars per year. ", "author": "Bullet3250", "created": 1787847372036, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Bullet3250", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Today - The United States and New Zealand remain the only two countries that permit this form of direct-to-consumer pharmaceutical advertising. ", "last_comment_created": 1787849986931, "content": "<p>1997: The <strong>FDA issued a clarification allowing ads to refer viewers to print materials or 1-800 numbers for full risk information, effectively ending the requirement to list all side effects on air.</strong>  This change triggered a massive surge in ad spending, which grew from $300 million in 1997 to over $1.5 billion by 2000.</p>\n<p>Today, Digital and TV Digital ad spending reaches over $30 Billion dollars per year.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 2, "score_up": 17, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATV3Om0gb", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 14, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "media", "id": 8802171, "raw_content": "", "author": "TaxDollarsHardAtWork", "created": 1787852570785, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "HumphreyPlowjogger", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "www.newsbusters.org", "is_crosspost"